# The image only needs package*.json + server/ (see Dockerfile). Everything
# else — installed deps, the client build, source, git, host-mode data — is
# excluded to keep the build context small and the image clean.
node_modules
dist
.git
.gitignore
index.html
vite.config.js
vercel.json
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
# Host-mode data stays out — except the packed map the renderer serves. The
# build is nixpacks (COPY . /app), so /api/cs3d can only find a pack that
# survives this file; excluding all of server/data ships the route with
# nothing behind it. Docker, unlike git, honours a negation inside an excluded
# directory, but the stepwise form is what buildkit reliably matches.
#
# This is fine for one 91 MB map. Before the other six land, move the packs to
# a volume (CS3D_PACK_DIR) or a bucket (VITE_CS3D_ASSET_BASE) and put the plain
# `server/data` line back — half a gig does not belong in a build context.
server/data/*
!server/data/cs3d
server/data/cs3d/*
!server/data/cs3d/pack
*.bat
.env
.env.*
*.md
